<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's BPSM no plans for Totta buyout.</title>
<headline>Portugal's BPSM no plans for Totta buyout.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Pinto &amp; Sotto Mayor has no intention of launching a public offer for sister bank Banco Totta &amp; Acores, the chairman of both banks said in a statement.</p>
<p>Luis Champalimaud, son of businessman Antonio Champalimaud whose group controls the banks, was echoing an earlier declaration by his father.</p>
<p>In his statement, Luis Champalimaud asked Portugal's Financial Markets Committee (CMVM) to lift the trade suspension on both shares.</p>
</text>
